------- FILE musicdrv_c.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  07c2					      include	"musicdrv_c.asm"	; the Frak tune, compact (atarivcs/music), 13 bytes of RAM at MUSRAM
      1  07c2							; Frak music driver, compact: the same tune and sound as musicdrv.asm (equiv_test.py compares
      2  07c2							; their register writes frame by frame), from frakmusic_c.inc (compact.py), with one routine for
      3  07c2							; both channels. Called once per frame (in vertical blank or overscan).
      4  07c2							;
      5  07c2							;   jsr MusicInit	 ; once
      6  07c2							;   jsr MusicTick	 ; every frame
      7  07c2							;
      8  07c2							; A pattern is a list of one-byte notes: bits 0-5 the code, bits 6-7 the length (8, 16, 24 or 32
      9  07c2							; frames). Codes: below SLIDE0 a note (MusNote: AUDF in bits 0-4, bit 7 set for AUDC 4, else 12),
     10  07c2							; SLIDE0 on a pitch slide (MusSlide: its offset into MusSlides, one pitch a frame, ended by $FF:
     11  07c2							; the last pitch is held), 61 tie (carry on, no new attack), 62 end of pattern, 63 rest. Each
     12  07c2							; channel has an order list in MusOrder (ended by $FF) and a loop position (MusLoop). A new note
